g viewBox="0 0 1000 1000" class="icon" height="1em" width="1em"><path d="m250 850l-187 0-63 0 0-62 0-188 63 0 0 188 187 0 0 62z m688 0l-188 0 0-62 188 0 0-188 62 0 0 188 0 62-62 0z m-875-938l0 188-63 0 0-188 0-62 63 0 187 0 0 62-187 0z m875 188l0-188-188 0 0-62 188 0 62 0 0 62 0 188-62 0z m-125 188l-1 0-93-94-156 156 156 156 92-93 2 0 0 250-250 0 0-2 93-92-156-156-156 156 94 92 0 2-250 0 0-250 0 0 93 93 157-156-157-156-93 94 0 0 0-250 250 0 0 0-94 93 156 157 156-157-93-93 0 0 250 0 0 250z" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 850)"></path></svg></a></div><div class="modebar-group"><a rel="tooltip" class="modebar-btn" data-title="Save plot as PNG" data-toggle="false" data-gravity="n"><svg viewBox="0 0 1000 1000" class="icon" height="1em" width="1em"><path d="m500 450c-83 0-150-67-150-150 0-83 67-150 150-150 83 0 150 67 150 150 0 83-67 150-150 150z m400 150h-120c-16 0-34 13-39 29l-31 93c-6 15-23 28-40 28h-340c-16 0-34-13-39-28l-31-94c-6-15-23-28-40-28h-120c-55 0-100-45-100-100v-450c0-55 45-100 100-100h800c55 0 100 45 100 100v450c0 55-45 100-100 100z m-400-550c-138 0-250 112-250 250 0 138 112 250 250 250 138 0 250-112 250-250 0-138-112-250-250-250z m365 380c-19 0-35-16-35-35 0-19 16-35 35-35 19 0 35 16 35 35 0 19-16 35-35 35z" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 850)"></path></svg></a><a rel="tooltip" class="modebar-btn" data-title="Open in dialog (edit layout)" data-toggle="false" data-gravity="n"><svg viewBox="0 0 1000 1000" class="icon" height="1em" width="1em"><path d="M786 296v-267q0-15-11-26t-25-10h-214v214h-143v-214h-214q-15 0-25 10t-11 26v267q0 1 0 2t0 2l321 264 321-264q1-1 1-4z m124 39l-34-41q-5-5-12-6h-2q-7 0-12 3l-386 322-386-322q-7-4-13-4-7 2-12 7l-35 41q-4 5-3 13t6 12l401 334q18 15 42 15t43-15l136-114v109q0 8 5 13t13 5h107q8 0 13-5t5-13v-227l122-102q5-5 6-12t-4-13z" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 850)"></path></svg></a></div></div></div><svg class="main-svg" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" width="700" height="383.328"><g class="hoverlayer"></g></svg></div></div></div></foreignObject></g><g transform="translate(470,20)" x="470" y="20" title="codeHTML" width="560" height="531" class="codeHTML" name="codeHTML" rot="0"><foreignObject x="0" y="0" width="560" height="531" style="width: 560px; height: 531px;"><div name="htmlCode" style="zoom: 0.56; height: 948.214px; width: 1000px;" code="&lt;div class=&quot;ch&quot;&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;8-bit ADC and DAC joined by a Bus&lt;/h1&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;ch-card&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Circuit Components&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Source (V1):&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;em&gt;SinVoltage&lt;/em&gt;, 2.5 V &amp;plusmn; 2.4 V at 1 kHz: a sine wave that stays inside the 0 &amp;hellip; 5 V range of the converters&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADC (U1):&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;em&gt;ADC_analog&lt;/em&gt;, 8 bits, V&lt;sub&gt;ref&lt;/sub&gt; = 5 V. Input &lt;em&gt;ain&lt;/em&gt; = node &lt;em&gt;vin&lt;/em&gt;; the 8 outputs are on the bus pin &lt;em&gt;D[0:7]&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DAC (U2):&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;em&gt;DAC_analog&lt;/em&gt;, 8 bits, V&lt;sub&gt;ref&lt;/sub&gt; = 5 V. Its bus pin &lt;em&gt;D[0:7]&lt;/em&gt; receives the 8 bits; the output &lt;em&gt;aout&lt;/em&gt; drives the load&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Load (R1):&lt;/strong&gt; 10 k&amp;Omega; to ground&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;The bus&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The thick wire between the converters is named &lt;strong&gt;D[0:7]&lt;/strong&gt; (Reference in the Properties panel) and both pins carry the same name: a bus of 8 lines, &lt;em&gt;D0&lt;/em&gt; (LSB) to &lt;em&gt;D7&lt;/em&gt; (MSB). The pins and the wire have the same width, so they are connected. If the widths differed, the pin would show the green square of an unconnected pin.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In the generated code the bus pin becomes the list of its nodes, as the models expect:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ch-formula&quot;&gt;
U1 = ADC_analog(&quot;vin&quot;, [&quot;D0&quot;, &quot;D1&quot;, &quot;D2&quot;, &quot;D3&quot;, &quot;D4&quot;, &quot;D5&quot;, &quot;D6&quot;, &quot;D7&quot;])&lt;br&gt;
U2 = DAC_analog([&quot;D0&quot;, &quot;D1&quot;, &quot;D2&quot;, &quot;D3&quot;, &quot;D4&quot;, &quot;D5&quot;, &quot;D6&quot;, &quot;D7&quot;], &quot;aout&quot;)
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Every line is an ordinary node: &lt;em&gt;D7&lt;/em&gt; and &lt;em&gt;D0&lt;/em&gt; can be plotted, or used by any other element, just by writing their name.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Principle&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ADC computes the code of the input, and the DAC rebuilds a voltage from the code:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ch-formula&quot;&gt;
$\text{code} = \left\lfloor \dfrac{V_{in}}{V_{ref}}\, 2^N \right\rfloor \qquad V_{out} = V_{ref}\,\dfrac{\text{code}}{2^N}$
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With N = 8 and V&lt;sub&gt;ref&lt;/sub&gt; = 5 V one step (LSB) is 5/256 = &lt;strong&gt;19.5 mV&lt;/strong&gt;. The output is a staircase that follows the input from below: the difference V&lt;sub&gt;in&lt;/sub&gt; &amp;minus; V&lt;sub&gt;out&lt;/sub&gt; stays between 0 and 1 LSB.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;ch-grid&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ch-col blue&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Results (0 &amp;hellip; 2 ms)&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Input &lt;em&gt;vin&lt;/em&gt;: &lt;strong&gt;0.10 V to 4.90 V&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Output &lt;em&gt;aout&lt;/em&gt;: &lt;strong&gt;0.098 V to 4.882 V&lt;/strong&gt;, 113 different levels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;V&lt;sub&gt;in&lt;/sub&gt; &amp;minus; V&lt;sub&gt;out&lt;/sub&gt;: &lt;strong&gt;1.4 mV to 18.6 mV&lt;/strong&gt; (mean 10 mV, i.e. half an LSB)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;D7&lt;/em&gt; is high (5 V) while &lt;em&gt;vin&lt;/em&gt; is above 2.5 V (the MSB of the code)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ch-col green&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Things to try&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plot &lt;em&gt;D0&lt;/em&gt; or &lt;em&gt;D6&lt;/em&gt;: the lower the bit, the faster it toggles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Change V&lt;sub&gt;ref&lt;/sub&gt; of both converters (e.g. 3.3 V) and the amplitude of the source&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use 4 bits: rename the pins and the wire to &lt;em&gt;D[0:3]&lt;/em&gt; (steps of 0.31 V)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Raise the source above V&lt;sub&gt;ref&lt;/sub&gt;: the ADC clips at code 255&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
"> 
    <!-- Parent container that responds to mouse movement -->
    <div class="chtool"> 
        
        <!-- tool bar-->
        <div class="ch-page-toolbar" style="zoom: 1.78571;">
            <button class="ch-toolbar-button" title="Home">
                <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
                    <path d="M12 3 L3 10 V21 H9 V15 H15 V21 H21 V10 Z"></path>
                </svg>
            </button>
            <button class="ch-toolbar-button" title="Modified" onclick="modifyAction()">
                <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
